From fcb277fe8af67cf6c53592a49c2c6aac3abe9922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:16:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix: run the precapture task at its configured tumble
 rate, and rebuild the oracle

_select_phase2_stage returns early for the precapture task, so the episode kept
the constructor's target_tumble_scale (0.5) and ran at 0.1031 rad/s while
precapture_planning_environment_config asked for 0.20 * 0.20616 = 0.0412 -- the
frozen S1-v2 rate every other number in this project is measured at. At 0.1031
rad/s sustained co-rotation costs m*omega^2*r = 1.13 N per metre, so the 5 N
per-axis authority runs out at 4.4 m and the 8.66 N body diagonal at 7.7 m: the
outer region was not hard, it was actuator-infeasible, which is what the 8-9 m
MPC stall was measuring.

The coast-then-match oracle is rebuilt on three defects the failing run exposed:

- per-axis clipping of an over-scaled request rotated the applied force away
  from the commanded direction, turning saturation into an outward spiral;
  forces are now scaled by the largest normalised component, and the
  feedforward is served before the feedback where the box binds;
- the rotating-frame laws had no centrifugal, Coriolis or Euler feedforward, so
  the servo had to raise the whole co-rotation bias from tracking error at a
  gain (0.8 /s) whose linear range was 0.06 m/s;
- the match interpolated the direction forwards in the body frame, which has to
  sweep whatever angle the target turned through during the window (1.6 rad
  over 40 s) and demanded 0.0545 m/s^2 against the 0.0472 m/s^2 one axis can
  guarantee. The match is now integrated backwards from the moment the body
  axis is where the plan needs it, ramping the rate instead of the angle:
  0.0116 m/s^2 for the same endpoint.

Oracle acceptance on seed block 262000, 5 episodes: 5/5 completed with zero
truth violations, equivalent delta-v 1.51-2.58 m/s, mean force 0.70-1.71 N,
worst normalised margin +0.148, worst FOV margin +0.710 rad, 159.5-239.5 s.
All five gate checks pass.

The pre-fix logs/precapture_planning_baseline/*.json were measured at 0.1031
rad/s and cannot be compared with anything produced after this commit.

